{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "03NV", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-site-fpqc}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3bf51fa45d67d915d50e87c88603753381f18da8f5d1e7e0a0817324bd5e6eb5", "source_text": "The collection of fpqc coverings on the category of schemes\nsatisfies the axioms of site.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e1d70ed30e2facd8566ce932b30afc8d78ddb88abf7b918657e6d962b3769055", "unit_id": "tag:03NZ:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "03NV", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{topologies-lemma-fpqc}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6490f2be8b8f4035dfc6f098dce0bb6f28fe37e5e135698a9020dfe6050a8f86", "source_text": "See Topologies, Lemma <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bf46abbdb3c1a0c9e7cd6f1379076750d3d7d04a5edbad791b6deae82fbf75db", "unit_id": "tag:03NZ:proof"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03NV", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{topologies-section-fpqc}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e5e05c46e0c3fe6e8b7bd903115e8e6852012948d06cbf9895d19710298b22f6", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIt seems that this lemma allows us to define the fpqc site of the category\nof schemes. However, there is a set theoretical problem that comes up when\nconsidering the fpqc topology, see\nTopologies, Section <REF_0001>.\nIt comes from our requirement that sites are ``small'', but that no small\ncategory of schemes can contain a cofinal system of fpqc coverings of a\ngiven nonempty scheme. Although this does not strictly speaking prevent\nus from defining  ``partial'' fpqc\nsites, it does not seem prudent to do so. The work-around is to allow\nthe notion of a sheaf for the fpqc topology (see below) but to prohibit\nconsidering the category of all fpqc sheaves.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9bfc4fbe41b27812d08f8e4e7693291e82133b1ace509b4f90239f7fad3bc424", "unit_id": "tag:03NV:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "03NV", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Sch/S$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F} : (\\Sch/S)^{opp} \\to \\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\{U_i \\to U\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0007": "$S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{equation-sheaf-axiom}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-sheaf-property-fpqc}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:cdd5f06b0e3f4853799b418033b32ee375c4f7f288c0398e329de86cf45af86f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:926bb559c653fdb48498028fccb2776646d9767e74ba27c11b4348c14ac4ce28", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. The category of schemes over <MATH_0002> is denoted\n<MATH_0003>. Consider a functor\n<MATH_0004>, in other words\na presheaf of sets. We say <MATH_0005>\n<TEXTITOPEN_0001>satisfies the sheaf property for the fpqc topology<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nif for every fpqc covering <MATH_0006> of schemes over <MATH_0007>\nthe diagram (<REF_0001>) is an equalizer diagram.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1a8217a43f3beeea79112078d9bf46902d2f924de1e8038ea55e13721e49c127", "unit_id": "tag:03X6:statement"}
